      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This study employs a precision-engineered AAV9-delivered, capped Cas9 protein to facilitate targeted cleavage of the glycine-glutamic acid (Glu6Val) mutation in the human β-globin (HBB) locus within human hematopoietic stem and progenitor cells. Following lentiviral transduction for stable integration of a doxycycline-inducible gRNA expression cassette, cord blood units undergo electrolytic transfection to deliver the ribonucleoprotein complex into CD34+ precursors under serum-free conditions. The engineered cells are subsequently expanded in granulocyte-macrophage colony-stimulating factor (GM-CSF)-enriched media for 14 days to ensure full hematopoietic reconstitution prior to autologous intravenous infusion.",
      "source": "target",
